# Z word on G5/G5.1 (BEZIER_Z_LINEAR) and exact G93 (BEZIER_EXACT_INVERSE_TIME).
# Numbers in [] are catalog IDs from ../../README.md. Every accepted curve is
# checked for a Z that never reverses and is linear in the length travelled
# (BEZIER_Z_LINEAR 2) or in the segment number (1); zlen and zarc pin numbers.

# ---- end point and modes [50] ------------------------------------------------

= [50] Z word: G5 ends exactly at Z @z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z-1 I3 J3 P3 Q3
pos -90 -100 -11

= [50] Z word: G5.1 ends exactly at Z @z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5.1 X10 Y0 Z2.5 I5 J5
pos -90 -100 -7.5

= [50] Z up and down along a chain, implicit I/J @z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z3 I3 J3 P3 Q-3
G5 X20 Y0 Z-3 P3 Q3
G5 X30 Y0 P3 Q-3
pos -70 -100 -13

= [50] Z in G91 and inches @z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G91 G5 X10 Y0 Z-1 I3 J3 P3 Q3
G5 X10 Y0 Z-1 P3 Q3
pos -80 -100 -12
G20 G5 X1 Y0 Z0.1 P0.1 Q0.1
pos -54.6 -100 -9.46

= [50] Z from a work offset far from the Z origin @z
G10 L2 P1 X0 Y0 Z-300
G0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z0.05 I3 J3 P3 Q3
pos 10 0 -299.95

= [50] Z word outside the travel plane only with G17 @z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G18 G5 X10 Y0 Z-1 I3 J3 P3 Q3 -> error
G19 G5.1 X10 Y0 Z-1 I5 J5 -> error
pos -100 -100 -10

# ---- Z against the path [51] --------------------------------------------------

# A straight line with both control points at its end: the parameter
# covers most of the length early, so Z by parameter runs far ahead.
= [51] handles 99:1 on a straight line, Z by length @zlen
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X100 Y0 Z10 I99 J0 P1 Q0
zlen 0 1e-5
zarc 0 1e-4

= [51] handles 99:1 on a straight line, Z by parameter is off by a third of the travel @z @!zlen
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X100 Y0 Z10 I99 J0 P1 Q0
zarc 0.3 0.45

= [51] both handles at the start, quadratic with a far control point @zlen
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5.1 X10 Y0 Z-4 I40 J60
zlen 0 1e-5
zarc 0 2e-3
G5 X0 Y0 Z4 I0 J0 P30 Q30
zlen 0 1e-5
zarc 0 2e-3

= [51] loop and cusp: Z keeps climbing through the crossing @zlen
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z5 I20 J10 P10 Q10
zlen 0 1e-5
G5 X0 Y0 Z-5 I10 J10 P10 Q10
zlen 0 1e-5

= [51] symmetric arch: both variants within a tenth of the travel @z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z1 I-3 J3 P3 Q3
zarc 0 0.1

# ---- float accumulation [52] --------------------------------------------------

# The length is summed in single precision over every segment, twice. At the
# cap that is 2000 additions of chords from 0.0002 mm to 30 mm.
= [52] 2000 segments: the running length stays on the line @zlen
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 Z50 I100000 J0 P1 Q50000
zlen 0 1e-5
G5 X0 Y0 Z-50 I0.01 J0 P100000 Q7
zlen 0 1e-5

= [52] 2000 segments far from the origin @zlen
G10 L2 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G0 X60000 Y-60000 Z-1000
F1000
G5 X60010 Y-60000 Z-1001 I30000 J0 P1 Q30000
zlen 0 2e-3

= [52] Z travel of one step on a long curve @zlen
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X300 Y0 Z0.004 I100 J100 P100 Q100

# ---- degenerate curves [53] ---------------------------------------------------

= [53] all points coincide: a plain Z move, nothing divided by zero @z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X0 Y0 Z-3 I0 J0 P0 Q0
pos -100 -100 -13

= [53] closed curve with Z @z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X0 Y0 Z2 I10 J0 P0 Q10
pos -100 -100 -8

= [53] curve shorter than a step with a long Z @z
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X0.001 Y0 Z8 I0.001 J0.001 P0.001 Q0.001
pos -99.999 -100 -2

# ---- exact G93 [39] [54] ------------------------------------------------------

= [39] G93 G5 takes 1/F minutes @g93
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G93
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 F2

= [39] G93 G5.1 takes 1/F minutes @g93
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G93
G5.1 X10 Y0 I5 J5 F2

= [54] G93 with Z: the time covers the 3D length @g93
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G93
G5 X10 Y0 Z-20 I3 J3 P3 Q3 F2
G5.1 X20 Y0 Z0 I5 J5 F0.5

= [54] G93 with unequal segments and at the cap @g93
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G93
G5 X100 Y0 Z10 I99 J0 P1 Q0 F4
G5 X110 Y0 Z50 I100000 J0 P1 Q50000 F0.01

= [54] G93 pure Z move through G5 @g93
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G93
G5 X0 Y0 Z-3 I0 J0 P0 Q0 F2
pos -100 -100 -13

= [54] G93 does not leak: G94 after the curve, G1 in G93 @g93
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
G93
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3 F2
G1 X20 F2
G94
F1000
G5 X30 Y0 Z1 I3 J3 P3 Q3
pos -70 -100 -9
